<resources>
    <!-- Build #87 (Casey Nov 23): BLUE / WHITE scheme, like the maps.
         The vivid-LED-orange primary is gone — Casey: "not digging all
         the orange and green… going with a scheme similar to the maps…
         blues and whites… only a small amount of red yellow orange and
         green where appropriate." Primary is now bright blue #00b4ff
         (the map's route blue) on plain black #080808, with white text.
         The map keeps its deep navy #07172f base. Steel blue #5a7aa8 is the secondary accent.
         Warm colours survive ONLY where the colour MEANS something and
         only in small amounts: red = over-limit / error / destructive,
         green = locked / good / done / Start, yellow = degraded / warn.
         The dead orange definitions (amber, amberDeep, amberBrick,
         ember, glow) are removed — nothing referenced them. -->
    <color name="bg">#080808</color>
    <color name="blue">#00b4ff</color>
    <color name="blueLight">#7dd3ff</color>
    <color name="steelBlue">#5a7aa8</color>
    <color name="mapNavy">#07172f</color>
    <color name="text">#f5f5f5</color>
    <color name="muted">#bbbbbb</color>
    <color name="chrome">#f0f0f0</color>
</resources>
